WEBVTT

00:00:46.510 --> 00:00:48.450
Christian in the morning, election room central,

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:52.550
polls have closed, the people have spoken.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:56.910
I think we have ourselves a new mayor-elect, Cicely.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:01:00.000
I know some returns are just coming in from coffee,

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.190
mountain. But according to our early tallies and early exit polls, Cave Bear

00:01:07.190 --> 00:01:12.960
predicts the new winner to be, ta-da, Mary Margaret O'Connell.

00:01:16.710 --> 00:01:20.510
Congratulations, my dear. The better man was a woman.

00:01:20.510 --> 00:01:24.670
Ah, thanks, Walt. Citizens of Sicily, I'd like to

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:30.000
compliment the last of the clean campaigners. To the shrewdest, toughest

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:35.030
Most decent political opponent I've ever had the pleasure of being trounced by.

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.030
Very nice.

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.030
Well spoken.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:38.070
You got a lot of grub on it.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:39.530
No, there's plenty. Help yourself.

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:40.530
Thank you.

00:01:41.630 --> 00:01:43.710
Hey, Walt. Sorry you lost.

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.830
Didn't really want some job anyway, Ed.

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:49.610
Of course, the stationery would have been nice.

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:50.810
And the occasional junket.

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.150
Yeah.

00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:54.490
And I hope you understood my backing, Walt.

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.500
Oh, sure. Everything's fair in love and politics.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.000
But I will be looking for your future support on the council, though.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:06.160
Hey.

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.790
Look, I realize it's a little early to be worrying about an agenda,

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:12.090
but I just made my first dump run this morning.

00:02:12.530 --> 00:02:15.830
I can't believe how far you people have to drive just to get rid of your trash.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.010
Well, the upside, though, is you don't have to listen to those garbage trucks at 5 a.m.

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:19.350
Yeah.

00:02:19.690 --> 00:02:21.270
Well, I was just thinking.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:25.090
I don't know why the town doesn't just have a central dumpster.

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:26.970
Cut way down on the trips people make.

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.150
You know, it's funny you should mention that,

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.000
because that exact...

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.380
idea was brought up during the public meeting last January, during the cold snap, right after

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:39.120
they found Buford Minto, solid as a popsicle, 100 feet from the dump with a hefty bag in

00:02:39.120 --> 00:02:47.750
each hand. Wow. Here's our boy. Here we go. That boy. Huh? Come here. Yeah. You believe

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.310
this rascal? Fought off an attacking bull moose in the talk race of champions. 30 below,

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:56.850
half the field scratched, all he does is turn around and lead his team to a course record.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.680
Naturally, his racing days are behind him.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:02.130
-Pure husky, right?

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:04.420
-For generations. Monadnock line.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.740
Pedigree like the Windsors of Buckingham, only less inbreeding.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.160
-What's his dead fee?

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:12.990
-Oh, I've gotten as much as $500 and never less than three.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:14.810
-What are you selling him for?

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:19.050
-Oh, I shouldn't be selling him at all, but I'm letting him go at five large.

00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:21.150
-$5,000?

00:03:21.150 --> 00:03:28.270
-Oh, you handle him right. You can be whole again inside a year, and after that, he's a cash cow.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:30.000
-How many times has he sired?

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:33.250
Let's just say, he's never home on a Saturday night.

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:34.300
Is that it?

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:37.490
Is that right?

00:03:37.490 --> 00:03:42.920
Members of the City Council, it is a great pleasure to formally introduce to you our

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.090
newly elected Mayor, Ms. Maggie O'Connor.

00:03:46.090 --> 00:03:47.090
Hear, hear.

00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.090
Welcome, Maggie.

00:03:48.090 --> 00:03:49.090
Good to have you aboard.

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:51.600
Thank you, Councilor.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:58.330
Well, okay, first of all, um, allow me to say that I realize this is not a formal public

00:03:58.330 --> 00:04:00.000
meeting, but Michelle has requested permission.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.700
- Permission to cover it for, uh, Maurice's paper.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.060
Any objections?

00:04:04.060 --> 00:04:05.240
- Can't see anything wrong.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.470
- It's okay with me.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.940
- Great, so ruled.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:13.120
Well, let's get down to business.

00:04:13.120 --> 00:04:14.850
Council will come to order.

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.850
Okay, the agenda calls for debate

00:04:20.850 --> 00:04:23.690
on Council Bill R-433.

00:04:23.690 --> 00:04:25.810
Now, as this relates to resource conservation,

00:04:25.810 --> 00:04:28.510
I'd like to start with a related subject.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.000
It's crazy that each of us has

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.620
drive our own trash out to the fill.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:35.620
I don't think any of us wants to move the dump to town, Your Honor.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.380
Oh, no, I'm talking about a dumpster.

00:04:37.950 --> 00:04:38.190
Oh.

00:04:38.570 --> 00:04:41.550
And when it fills up, a truck picks it up and empties it.

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:43.610
As soon as you bring in vehicles, you're talking big bucks.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.050
There just isn't a tax base for it.

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:49.550
There's a trucker in Sleep Mute who'll provide the service on a per-loaded basis.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:51.390
I think the mayor's on something.

00:04:51.470 --> 00:04:54.430
We could park a dumpster at the vacant lot on Hasbury.

00:04:54.570 --> 00:05:00.000
And I think my colleague and good friend Councilman Venkoor is showing his stripes again.

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:05.540
We're all aware of the Canadian's proclivity for socializing anything that moves.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:09.040
I think we should all confine our comments to the merits of the proposal.

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:12.680
I think it would behoove the Honourable Mayor to examine the city books.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:15.990
The Sicily Treasury couldn't afford to rent a Tonka truck.

00:05:15.990 --> 00:05:18.780
Isn't that right, Councilman Stevens?

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:22.870
Councilman Stevens?

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:27.400
The judicious expenditure of government resources can have a multiplying effect.

00:05:27.400 --> 00:05:28.940
Everybody will benefit.

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.000
Who's going to foot the bid?

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.860
for this esteemed gentleman's twenty-some bags a week I resent that okay

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:40.930
come to order with all due respect madam chairwoman I think you're going to find

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.830
an unbridgeable chasm between some of us on the question of government as social

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:55.670
panacea don't you agree councilman Stevens yes absolutely everybody knows

00:05:55.670 --> 00:06:00.000
where I stand on this issue the natural order of things moves along better

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.050
when unimpeded by artificial stimuli you can quote me on that the chair believes

00:06:05.050 --> 00:06:09.140
that the government has a responsibility to be constructive I mean if it's going

00:06:09.140 --> 00:06:13.800
to exist why shouldn't it promote the public good here here is this not what

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:17.950
the democratic process is all about at the next meeting expect a formal proposal

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:25.950
with hard numbers you should notice an improvement in the next two or three

00:06:25.950 --> 00:06:30.000
days okay so you just call me if you need a refill on that prescription alright take

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:59.960
care. Dr. Capra? Hey, this must be my new guy. Uh, excuse me, Marilyn. I don't want to get off on the wrong foot here, but really, this is no place for pets. He's not a pet. What do you mean? Well, the thing about Huskies, Dr. Capra, they're not like other dogs. They're work machines up here, practically public transportation. He's an investment. Marilyn doesn't even like dogs. She's a cat person. Well, maybe we could just keep them...

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:01.370
By the side of your desk there.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:04.290
What's his name?

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.030
Chuck.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:11.530
Hey, Chuck.

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.220
Well, what can I do for you, Ed?

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:17.540
Almost forgot.

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:18.720
Ruthown sent me over.

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:21.520
Got a letter for you.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.300
Just came in.

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:24.330
What is this?

00:07:27.490 --> 00:07:30.000
Dear Phil, what do you say to a round of golf Friday?

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.170
warmest regards Joel Fleischmann I didn't even know there was a golf course around here

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:38.970
Dr. Fleischmann's a pretty good duffer too do you know he once beat the club pro

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:43.590
I have to pitch and putt on Finger Lake where is Dr. Fleischmann exactly every time I

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:49.270
ask someone they change the subject Manonash Village where's that

00:07:49.270 --> 00:07:54.980
Hope River just past Dead Man's Gorge not a bad trip though if you make it before the ice flows start

00:08:10.520 --> 00:08:13.950
Isn't it? What's up?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:17.060
Nothing. Just out riding.

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.950
Took, uh, Umayak Road up to the dump.

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:22.720
6.4 miles each way.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:25.710
Look, if this is about to dust up at the council meeting, don't worry.

00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:28.710
We're not gonna lockstep on everything just 'cause we're friends.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:31.040
Something wrong?

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:31.540
No.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:33.930
I come in?

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:35.220
Yeah, sure.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:37.320
You want some tea or something?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:37.620
No.

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:40.070
Hey.

00:08:42.670 --> 00:08:48.110
Quite an inaugural outing today.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:50.140
Oh, yeah.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.610
You know, I don't know why everything got her nose so out of joint.

00:08:54.350 --> 00:08:55.660
I don't think I was unprofessional.

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:56.360
Do you?

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.940
Are you kidding?

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.730
You're born for this job.

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:05.340
The way your hands just fit around that gavel.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:07.440
The timbre of your voice.

00:09:08.010 --> 00:09:09.600
The way you called us to order.

00:09:10.370 --> 00:09:12.630
Your mastery of Robert's rules.

00:09:17.300 --> 00:09:20.660
I'm sorry.

00:09:24.440 --> 00:09:27.290
I won't.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:32.220
Chris, I want you to leave, okay?

00:09:33.110 --> 00:09:34.190
Come on, I want you to leave.

00:09:34.330 --> 00:09:34.570
Okay.

00:09:34.810 --> 00:09:35.030
Okay.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:35.910
Here.

00:09:36.280 --> 00:09:36.540
Come on.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:37.980
All right?

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:39.520
All right?

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:40.160
All right?

00:09:41.570 --> 00:09:43.550
Now, bye.

00:09:44.510 --> 00:09:45.580
See ya.

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:56.060
It's hard to believe there'd be a regulation course way out here.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.980
I wonder if the club has any kind of rest.

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:03.930
You want authentic Alaskan cuisine, Mananash is your place.

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:09.100
Great, but I wouldn't give for a nice salmon filet and a bottle of Sterling Chardonnay.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.810
This is Mananash.

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:24.530
This is Mananash? Are you sure?

00:10:31.750 --> 00:10:32.390
Dr. Capra.

00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:33.640
Oh, hello.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:35.530
Dr. Fleischman sent you?

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:37.190
Oh, I'm Dr. Fleischman.

00:10:39.100 --> 00:10:40.350
Oh.

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:41.590
Glad you could make it.

00:10:41.630 --> 00:10:42.130
How was the trip?

00:10:42.820 --> 00:10:43.220
Fine.

00:10:43.850 --> 00:10:44.490
Fine, yeah.

00:10:44.710 --> 00:10:50.770
I lost a nine iron and some choppy water about a mile back, but other than that, I'm just

00:10:50.770 --> 00:10:54.390
surprised that there's a golf course this far off the beaten path, you know.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:55.470
Yeah.

00:10:56.260 --> 00:10:58.000
Well, let's get your stuff and we'll head on out.

00:10:58.390 --> 00:10:58.930
Thanks, Dale.

00:10:59.090 --> 00:10:59.490
I got it.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:00.000
I got it.

00:11:00.320 --> 00:11:09.170
Good day for golf, huh?

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:17.260
Yeah, it's beautiful.

00:11:17.260 --> 00:11:20.260
What'd you say the bottom line is for a stud fee?

00:11:20.260 --> 00:11:21.690
$400?

00:11:21.690 --> 00:11:23.580
He usually gets $500.

00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.380
$500.

00:11:25.380 --> 00:11:28.450
Well, nice arctic coat.

00:11:30.570 --> 00:11:33.130
Those ears could be a little longer though.

00:11:33.130 --> 00:11:36.730
He's not a show dog, shorter ears are better for the cold.

00:11:36.730 --> 00:11:42.410
Ah, well walk him around for me.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:48.440
Too prancy, I bet he could cover some ground.

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:53.710
Yeah, Marilyn, looks like you've got a real champene there.

00:11:53.710 --> 00:11:56.400
Those pads could be a little thicker.

00:11:56.400 --> 00:12:00.000
He's farther than when I did a ride twice.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:04.000
Chuck makes beautiful music with my Countess, Casamissima.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:06.980
I could have a wheel dog that'll fill out my team.

00:12:08.210 --> 00:12:11.910
Well, let me take him and introduce the beautiful couple.

00:12:11.910 --> 00:12:14.370
I'll be back and write you a check.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:19.420
Come on.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:23.280
Say a minute, Penn and Chris.

00:12:23.280 --> 00:12:26.430
Chris?

00:12:26.430 --> 00:12:27.560
Yeah.

00:12:32.140 --> 00:12:43.240
I did something really crazy last night Ed. I did a triple gainer into the grand can of craziness. I made a pass at Maggie.

00:12:43.240 --> 00:13:00.000
Oh? Yeah. Of course she threw me out. I mean completely took her by surprise you know. She wasn't the only one. I don't know where it came from. It just blindsided me. I couldn't figure it out till now. You know what it was?

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:03.020
Nope.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:05.540
Who's the gavel?

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:06.560
The gavel?

00:13:06.560 --> 00:13:07.520
Yeah, her role, the mayor.

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:10.850
It's power.

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:12.340
It's authority.

00:13:12.340 --> 00:13:15.950
I don't know why I didn't figure it out 'til now.

00:13:15.950 --> 00:13:19.470
I always had this thing for powerful women.

00:13:19.470 --> 00:13:23.050
Kinda like it's hard, hardwired right to my lawn.

00:13:23.050 --> 00:13:24.050
You know what I'm sayin'?

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:27.340
Can you hand me a slotted screwdriver?

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:29.510
Yeah.

00:13:31.950 --> 00:13:34.840
Goes all the way back to the 9th grade.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.000
Mrs. Goad.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.190
Talk about a tight ship, absolute rule.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:43.900
Couldn't line my way into a hall pass no matter how hard I tried.

00:13:43.900 --> 00:13:45.700
Or when I got sent to jail.

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:49.840
When that judge sentenced me, 'cause I can see it right now.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:56.090
She's sitting there with that back erect, head cocked ever so slightly.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:14:00.000
That jet black robe setting off that alabaster skin.

00:14:01.500 --> 00:14:04.160
The Honorable Claire Dawson Chonderval.

00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:05.980
She's throwing a book at me, Ed,

00:14:05.980 --> 00:14:08.380
and all I want to do is suck those little white earlobes.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:11.300
Let me show you this.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:19.170
Here it is. Look at that.

00:14:19.980 --> 00:14:20.880
Time Magazine?

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:22.040
Janet Reno.

00:14:22.930 --> 00:14:24.730
That's the reason I couldn't throw this thing out, Ed.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:26.520
Now I understand.

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.570
All right, Doctor.

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:34.290
What about your clubs?

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:37.010
I manage pretty well with the shillelagh.

00:14:38.440 --> 00:14:40.480
Well, I must admit, every time I stare down at a par five,

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.560
I fantasize about one of those Callaway Warbirds.

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:43.220
Why?

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:44.240
Why, what do you got here?

00:14:44.840 --> 00:14:46.000
Graphite shafts.

00:14:46.340 --> 00:14:47.220
Carbon graphite.

00:14:47.520 --> 00:14:47.920
Nice.

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:50.900
Got a wedding tomorrow.

00:14:51.600 --> 00:14:51.880
Oh.

00:14:52.780 --> 00:14:53.360
Tell me.

00:14:54.340 --> 00:14:55.610
What do you think of Sicily?

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:56.850
It's pretty peaceful, huh?

00:14:57.540 --> 00:15:00.000
Well, I should have seen it before it was overbuilt.

00:15:01.530 --> 00:15:02.430
What's the gun for?

00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:07.890
High altitude migratory foul, maybe.

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:09.770
Pretty nice, huh?

00:15:11.010 --> 00:15:12.980
It's a new brownie.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:18.770
Got enough stopping power for anything we might come across.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:19.430
Not that we will.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:30.000
I want my money back, and I want it now.

00:15:30.600 --> 00:15:31.830
- What happened?

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.230
- It's what didn't happen that concerns me.

00:15:34.230 --> 00:15:35.870
Our agreement is null and void

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.010
based on his lack of performance.

00:15:38.010 --> 00:15:39.310
- He didn't do it?

00:15:39.310 --> 00:15:42.150
- Didn't, he might as well have been introduced

00:15:42.150 --> 00:15:44.410
to a brown rice cake for all the interest

00:15:44.410 --> 00:15:46.010
he showed in my bitch.

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.270
- Maybe it wasn't the right time.

00:15:48.270 --> 00:15:51.970
- Marilyn, the Countess was all over him

00:15:51.970 --> 00:15:54.450
like a cheap suit, all to no avail.

00:15:54.450 --> 00:15:56.660
He's nothing but a panty waist.

00:15:56.660 --> 00:15:58.030
- Did you feed him something?

00:15:58.030 --> 00:16:00.000
- He had no appetite of any kind.

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:03.590
Hmm, maybe he's scared him.

00:16:03.710 --> 00:16:06.870
The only thing that he's scared of is doing his carnal duty.

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:14.520
I'll write you a refund.

00:16:19.470 --> 00:16:20.450
Then there's Angie Mingus.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:27.240
I know that you suspect manure is, but I'm wondering if this vestibular neurectomy is what's called for.

00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:30.000
What with the, uh, debilitating vertigo.

00:16:30.060 --> 00:16:35.640
hearing loss yeah well you got one other option you know you can do a lab

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:49.250
